agent-sandbox
=============

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the files in this repository (Containerfiles,
scripts, configuration and documentation). It does not cover the software that
the container images are built from or download.

Third-party software in the images
----------------------------------
The images are built from Debian, Alpine and upstream releases. Each component
keeps its own license, for example:

  - Debian trixie and Alpine packages (incl. git, zsh, tinyproxy, iptables,
    GNU Octave and Octave Forge packages, Chromium, Mesa): various licenses,
    many GPL/LGPL. License texts are in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright
    (Debian) or the package metadata (Alpine). Sources are available from the
    Debian and Alpine archives.
  - Node.js (MIT and bundled licenses), Julia (MIT and bundled licenses),
    uv (MIT or Apache-2.0), Tailscale (BSD-3-Clause), ROCm (various).
    Sources are available from their upstream projects.

Claude Code and Codex
---------------------
Neither Claude Code nor the OpenAI Codex CLI is included in the images. The
claude-code and codex add-ons download them when a container starts. Claude
Code is subject to Anthropic's terms (https://www.anthropic.com/legal), Codex
to its license (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/openai/codex) and OpenAI's
terms. Both providers' APIs and logins are used under the terms of your own
account.

Design
------
The overall design (firewalled devcontainer for coding agents) is inspired by
Anthropic's reference devcontainer for Claude Code. No files were copied from it.

agent-sandbox is not an Anthropic or OpenAI product.
